# The build context is the workspace root, because the server depends on
# brain-core by path and a context of `server/` alone cannot see it. That makes
# this file matter more than it usually would: `target/` alone is eleven
# gigabytes, and without this every build ships it to the daemon before the
# first instruction runs.
#
# Read by both `docker build` and `podman build`.

target/
dist/
.git/
.github/

# The GTK shell and everything that only it needs. The image builds
# `--package brain-server`, which does not look at any of this.
src/
tests/
examples/
data/
packaging/
install.sh
uninstall.sh
test.sh
sync-check.sh

*.md
